+  past its own floor, so an idle consumer's motionless floor never accrues
+  time to charge the next arriving message with. Once the floor has been
+  stalled past `FloorAge` (default 15m) and the message being settled is the
+  one pinning it — the sequence immediately above the floor — `Settle`
+  captures the raw message and headers to the DLQ and Acks the original,
+  whatever its attempt count.
+
+  Acting on it automatically is still a heuristic over consumer-global state,
+  so it ships with `BreakerObserveOnly`: evaluate and report the trip, act on
+  nothing. Useful for measuring the trip rate against real traffic — idle
+  stretches, filtered streams, restarts, replica splits, a DLQ outage — before
+  letting the library Ack on its own.
 - **`backoff`** — the redelivery policy for transiently-failed deliveries: a
   `NakWithDelay` envelope — flat by default, optionally growing per delivery
   (`Factor`/`MaxDelay`) — bounded by MaxDeliver, with opt-in
