 684	// TestObserveFloorIgnoresACaughtUpConsumer is the false positive that makes
 685	// the difference between a poison remedy and a message shredder: a quiet
 686	// consumer's floor sits still because NOTHING ARRIVED, not because anything
 687	// is stuck. Crediting the next message to arrive with that idle time would
 688	// dead-letter it on its second delivery. The stall clock therefore runs only
 689	// while the consumer has delivered past its own floor, and starts when the
 690	// gap opens — not when the floor last moved.
