   521	// TestBreakerIsSelectiveUnderAMassTransient is the scenario that separates a
   522	// poison-message remedy from a mass dead-lettering engine, and the reason the
   523	// breaker rations itself.
   524	//
   525	// entiredb is down for an hour. Every message in flight fails, the floor is
   526	// stalled, and every one of them satisfies the breaker's conditions: above
   527	// the floor, failing longer than the threshold, past MinDeliveries. Left
   528	// unrationed the breaker would empty the consumer into the DLQ — which is
   529	// precisely the outcome a short ladder would produce, and therefore precisely
   530	// what the breaker exists to avoid. It must claim ONE message per stall
   531	// window instead.
